  "legacyId": "9649fa42-f80a-4c28-9682-95b62516fea8",
  "type": "problem",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "description": "<div><p>Stations form a circular route. At station i, you collect gas[i] units and must spend cost[i] units to reach the next station. Begin with an empty tank at one station and travel exactly one full lap, never letting the tank go below zero. Return the starting station's zero-based index, or -1 if no full lap is possible.</p><p>The inputs guarantee that if a feasible starting station exists, it is unique. Gas collected at a station is available before paying for the trip to the next one.</p><p><strong>Example 1</strong></p><pre>Input: gas = [1,2,3,4,5], cost = [3,4,5,1,2]\nOutput: 3</pre><p>Explanation: Starting at index 3 leaves enough fuel to cross the costly early stations.</p><p><strong>Example 2</strong></p><pre>Input: gas = [2,3,4], cost = [3,4,3]\nOutput: -1</pre><p>Explanation: The route consumes more fuel than all stations provide.</p><p><strong>Example 3</strong></p><pre>Input: gas = [5], cost = [4]\nOutput: 0</pre><p>Explanation: The only station supplies enough fuel for its single trip.</p><p><strong>Constraints</strong></p><ul><li>1 ≤ gas.length = cost.length ≤ 10,000.</li><li>0 ≤ gas[i], cost[i] ≤ 10,000.</li><li>There is at most one feasible starting index.</li></ul></div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def canCompleteCircuit(self, gas: List[int], cost: List[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the requested result.\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "var canCompleteCircuit = function(gas, cost) {\n    // your code here\n};\n"
  },
